#created by Duel Circuit - Yata Mags (Yata-Lock, 2004)
#era 2004
#tier Alley headliner (docs/dev/HEADLINERS-2026-11-01.md)
#about Chaos Emperor Dragon sends every card in both hands and on the field to the Graveyard; Sangan or Witch, sent with them, finds Yata-Garasu, and Yata's attack on an empty opponent skips every draw from then on.
#why Plays the 2004 texts of Chaos Emperor Dragon, Sangan and Witch of the Black Forest, which no list allows today, with Pot of Greed and Graceful Charity (Forbidden).
#source Built from Format Library deck 3432 (decks/history/chaos-yata.ydk, 41 cards as played): Shining Angels for LIGHTs in the Graveyard and more draw for the lock pieces, in place of the White Magical Hats, Wabokus and a Creature Swap; and three Chaos Emperor Dragons for Delinquent Duo and The Forceful Sentry (the one card over its list: the owner's exception, so the wipe comes up)
#originals Original card versions (pre-errata / Goat format) as played in its era.
#banlist TCG April 2004
#recipe chaos-yata
